-It's nice to be here.

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:18.267
-Thank you. I appreciate it.
We all appreciate it.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:19.501
I see all of y'all.
Thank you very much. Yeah.

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:20.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:23.734
Happy holidays to you
and the fam.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.200
What goes on
in Reese Witherspoon

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.467
in the holidays?

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:27.634
-Oh, gosh.

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.601
Well, lots of singing
of Christmas carols.

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:30.734
-Yes.
-I like --

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:31.934
-Are you --
What?

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.200
-Are you a caroler?
Do you go out and like?

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.834
-Oh, I mean,
I don't think so anymore

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.601
-Just in house.
-When I was a kid,

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.167
we used to go door-to-door.
-You did?

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:39.434
-Yeah.
-Oh, wow.

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:41.200
-I grew up going door-to-door,
but now I just

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.033
stay home and watch
Michael Bublé specials.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.400
[ Laughs ]-
That's what everyone does now.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.534
Yeah, exactly. Yeah.

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:49.133
-I love the Bubs.
-Are you? I love the Bubs,

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.801
-Wait, that sound like...
-Yeah, I know. It's weird.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:53.367
It sounded weirder when I said
it. I don't know why.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:55.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.267
We love the Bublé.
We love him.

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.434
-We love Michael Bublé.

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:59.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:02.033
What just --
what just happened?

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:04.334
-Why does this happen?
Sorry, it doesn't matter.

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:07.601
-I have a friend who calls
him Michael Bubs.

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:08.901
-The Bubs.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.667
-Because they know him,
but nobody calls him that.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.067
-No, I think you mean
like Justin Bieber --

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.934
-That was so weird.
You call Biebs the Bubs.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:14.968
-The Biebs.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:16.033
Justin Bieber
you call the Biebs,

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:17.467
Michael Bublé the Bubs.

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:18.767
No, you don't.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:21.300
-I love the Bubs.
Yeah, I mean...

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.100
-Maybe it's Bub-- Bublay.
Oh, my God.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.267
-Yeah, I love the Bublay.

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:26.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.200
-Quest, help.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.267
-No, no, no, no, no.
Help, I'm drowning.

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.400
Is it hot in here?
-No, please, please, please.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.534
Look, I want to talk to you
about because, you know,

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:37.767
I follow on on the socials...
-Oh, my God.

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.467
-...and I -- you're very --

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.601
you're very crafty.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.901
You love to cook.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:45.200
-I love a crafternoon, y'all.
-Oh, craft...

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.634
-When you craft
in the afternoons,

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:48.634
it's crafternoon.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:50.334
You're making up all sorts
of new words.

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:52.567
Crafternoon.
You have to trademark that.

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:54.200
-Oh, my gosh.
-But -- but you...

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.467
Look at this. This is you making
a gingerbread house.

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:57.901
-Oh, yeah.
-This crushes what

00:01:57.901 --> 00:02:00.400
I was making for my kid.
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.367
-It's a very special pattern,
and...

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.133
-That's so much fun.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:07.133
-Most of the materials
were eaten by the end.

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:08.467
That's what my kids do.
They do it,

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:09.701
and then they just wait
and they're,

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:10.868
"Can I just take that off?"

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:12.033
I go, "Just destroy it
and eat it."

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:13.534
-Just eat it, just eat it.
-Just go for it.

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:17.033
-I mean, did you -- was your mom
into a gingerbread house

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:19.100
when you were growing up
and, like, did that for you?

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.200
-Yeah. Well, we grew up
partially in Germany

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.400
because my dad
was in the military,

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.667
so we always had
gingerbread houses

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:26.467
and like German candies
and stuff like that.

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:27.634
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:29.934
-I had a family.
Katrina Wamsley, the Wamsleys,

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:31.767
and they would --
we would go over to their house

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:34.434
and her mom made all these
different pieces of the house

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:35.400
and had frosting for people.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.701
And were like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:38.267
And that was like --
like a tradition.

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.000
-Like a perfect mom.
-It was the best.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.133
I loved it. I go, "Oh, my gosh."
It was so cool.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:44.033
-Ms. Wamsley?
-Yeah, Ms. Wamsley, yeah.

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.667
-Making everybody's
childhood magical.

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:46.968
-Yeah, she just --
Yeah, she did, yeah.

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:50.367
I will say season
two of "Morning Show..."

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:51.834
-Aww, did you like it?

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.868
-I loved it.
-Oh, thank you.

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:55.667
-Not only liked it, loved it.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.033
-Thank you. It was fun.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:58.467
-You took it to the next level,

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.167
